  "documentation": {
    "summary": "Escher's Impossible Objects — a clockwise ascending loop",
    "layout": "A perimeter loop that ascends clockwise: north side height-1, east side height-2, south side height-3, west side height-4. Each step up feels locally valid — you're just climbing stairs. But when you complete the loop, you're impossibly back where you started at height-1. The center is a void or sunken area. Artifacts placed along the loop path. The spatial paradox IS the lesson: local coherence, global impossibility.",
    "spatial_pattern": "ascending_loop",
    "key_elements": [
      "Clockwise ascending perimeter: 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → back to 1",
      "Each side feels like a natural step up",
      "Completing the loop reveals the impossibility",
      "Central void — no shortcut through the paradox",
      "Escher staircase, Penrose triangle, Magritte pipe along the path"
    ]
  },
